<task id="202" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Pre-live-fire lessons audit + formalize PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES + design provisioning-run structure (blocker for task 186 E2E)</title>
    <phase>Pre-Live-Fire — Consolidate lessons + structural gaps before E2E ceremony</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Doc-heavy authoring task: audit + inventory of all captured-but-unapplied lessons across notes/*, then author (a) PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md machine-parseable YAML + rendered markdown, (b) provisioning-run structural specs, (c) punch list for task 203 (apply). No .cs modifications in this task; substantial code changes ride in task 203. Owner directive 2026-08-24: "for point 1 - AND these need to be actually documented somewhere that can then feed into the process; this needs to be formalized e.g., a file, an app, a table--something that is codified" — this task is that codification.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-file audit + design synthesis + authoring formalized codified structure. Volume of source material (90+ notes files, 3 major docs at ~4000 lines total, skill file at 1092 lines) benefits from Opus's larger context + design-synthesis strength. Not xhigh — this is authoring/synthesis, not brownfield root-cause.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Serial: 202 audits + produces punch list → 203 (apply, potentially FULL rigor with .cs changes + skill updates) → 186 (E2E live-fire). 202 also touches .claude/patterns/provisioning/ scaffolding + potentially seeds .claude/skills/provision-environment/refs/ — main-session-only per Sub-Agent Write Boundary.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>200, 201</deps>
    <tags>lessons-learned, provisioning, l3-skill, docs, root-claude, skill-directives</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-10 hours (audit spans 90+ notes files; formalization requires design synthesis)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Consolidate every captured-but-unapplied lesson from projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/ (SESSION 2 fresh-sub F1-F20+, SESSION 3-4 handoff decisions, SESSION 5 IActionSeam + F20-chain, task-XXX-deviations notes, wave drift notes) into a single punch list mapped to landing spots (code / ArchTest / skill / design.md / deployment guide / new PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md). Author PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md as a formalized codified file (YAML for skill Step 0.5 consumption + rendered markdown for humans) enumerating every prerequisite outside provisioning automation (SPE container-types, Office add-in Entra apps, Copilot bot apps, Power BI SPs, Azure subscription creation, OpenAI TPM quota bumps for frontier models, resource-provider registration on fresh subs). Design the provisioning-runs/{customerId}-{runId}/ project structure mirroring coding-project pattern: {CLAUDE.md, intake.md, prerequisites-check.md, preflight-report.md, handler-log.md, manual-gates.md, handoff-report.md, lessons-learned.md} + provisioning-runs/INDEX.md cross-run registry + .claude/patterns/provisioning/ scaffolding for cross-run shared patterns. Do NOT apply the lessons in this task — that's task 203's scope. Output: a machine-parseable punch list at notes/task-202-punch-list.md that task 203 executes against.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform architect. Expert in: this project's r1 domain (customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1 spec.md + design.md v3.6); the /provision-environment L3 skill (1092 lines, Step 0-7 flow); coding-project structural pattern (projects/{name}/{spec,plan,design,CLAUDE.md,current-task,tasks/,notes/}) that this task adapts to provisioning-runs; the ADR-032 asymmetric-registration anti-pattern (root CLAUDE.md §10 F.1); the two-level lessons process (in-flight direct-apply vs project-close lessons-learned.md) per root CLAUDE.md §7 wrap-up + task-execute Step 11. Familiar with SESSION 5 (2026-08-24) manual-BFF-patching learnings + owner directive to codify prereqs.</role>

  <goal>Files exist and the following contracts are satisfied: (a) `docs/guides/PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md` authored as formalized codified reference (markdown-with-YAML-frontmatter OR markdown-plus-sibling-YAML at scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml — pick one and justify), enumerating every manual prerequisite with how-to + frequency (once-per-tenant / once-per-sub / once-per-env / once-per-customer) + programmatic-check recipe where possible; (b) design memo at notes/provisioning-run-structure-design.md specifying the provisioning-runs/{customerId}-{runId}/ folder layout + purpose of each artifact + template contents for CLAUDE.md/intake.md/handoff-report.md/lessons-learned.md; (c) design memo at notes/provisioning-run-agent-autonomy-design.md capturing the interactive-vs-autonomous split (what stays operator-interactive: SPE 24h wait detection, admin-consent verification; what can auto-advance: idempotent re-runs, backoff-poll of L2 REST); (d) punch list at notes/task-202-punch-list.md — machine-parseable table of every unapplied lesson × landing spot × effort estimate × dependency chain, sortable by "must-do-before-E2E" vs "can-do-after-E2E"; (e) proposed .claude/patterns/provisioning/ scaffolding (empty folder OR skeleton .md files with headers only — task 203 fills content); (f) update task 186's escalation triggers section: add explicit "if a lesson from task-202-punch-list.md was not applied before invocation, abort and defer to task 203" gate; (g) update project current-task.md + TASK-INDEX.md with task 202 completion status + explicit link to punch list.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Owner directive 2026-08-24 SESSION 5 conversation: "for point 1 - AND these need to be actually documented somewhere that can then feed into the process; this needs to be formalized e.g., a file, an app, a table--something that is codified". SESSION 5 attempted to boot Model 1 Prod BFF by patching individual App Service settings (5 gates cleared: Cosmos endpoint, CORS origins, DocumentIntelligence enable, Dataverse ServiceUrl, plus code fix e3a15db91 for IActionSeam ADR-032 asymmetric-registration bug). Owner recognized this was symptom-fixing, not project-relevant E2E validation. Corrective sequence: audit + apply all captured-but-unapplied lessons BEFORE invoking task 186 E2E ceremony, so live-fire proves the platform's automation rather than iterating through fail-cycles. Task 202 = the audit + formalization; task 203 = the apply.

**Two-level lessons process** (per SESSION 5 conversation resolution):
1. **NOW (retrospective)**: this task 202 + follow-on task 203 apply everything known. Goal: no known unapplied lesson when task 186 fires.
2. **ONGOING (forward-looking)**: skill Step 7 mandatory postmortem writing per-run `lessons-learned.md`; cross-run audit reads all lessons files periodically. This task designs the ONGOING structure; task 203 implements it in the skill.

**Prerequisite scope from owner** (SESSION 5): "container types are prerequisites — don't touch them, they live outside provisioning automation. Other prerequisites that are more appropriately handled outside provisioning automation" — codify list. Enumerate against the actual `az` + Power Platform inventory + design.md § shared-vs-dedicated split.

**Provisioning-run project structure directive from owner** (SESSION 5): "shouldn't there be a project structure within which a new environment provisioning project runs?" — YES. Mirror coding-project pattern; each provisioning run becomes an auditable mini-project.</background>
