  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner directive 2026-08-24 SESSION 5">PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md MUST be formalized codified — file/YAML/table — not just prose. Consumers: (a) /provision-environment Step 0.5 (task 203 wires the read), (b) human operators.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner directive 2026-08-24 SESSION 5">Provisioning-run structure MUST parallel coding-project structure (CLAUDE.md + spec-analog + tasks-analog + notes/ + lessons-learned). Auditable per-run; cross-run registry INDEX.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3 Sub-Agent Write Boundary">Sub-agents CANNOT write to .claude/ paths. Main session writes .claude/patterns/provisioning/ scaffolding.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §7 wrap-up test-diet gate">Do NOT invoke /test-diet in this task (no tests added/modified in 202 — pure docs + design memos).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 Component Justification">PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md is a NEW file — justify per §11 three-question template in the file header: (1) existing overlap with SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md §2? (yes, but not codified/machine-parseable — the deployment guide is prose narrative for humans; PREREQUISITES is codified data for skill + humans); (2) can extend the deployment guide instead? (partially — the codified list belongs alongside human narrative for tool consumption); (3) concrete failure without? (skill Step 0.5 cannot programmatically verify prereqs → operator hits F1-F9-class errors during Step 2 preflight instead of Step 0.5 fail-fast).</constraint>
    <constraint source="this project design.md §6.5 ADR Tensions">If audit surfaces architectural gaps requiring ADR amendment (e.g., SESSION 5 Lesson 3: multi-tenant Dataverse routing), file as ADR Tension in design.md via path A/B/C protocol — do NOT bypass. Task 203 applies the resolution.</constraint>
