  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (STANDARD, high effort, opus tier). Read the 4 authoritative reference files (spec.md v3.6, design.md v3.6, deployment guide, /provision-environment SKILL.md) + the top-priority lessons file (lessons-learned-model1-prod-standup-2026-08-22.md, 870 lines). Skim SESSION 5 handoff in current-task.md for the 4 lessons captured live.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Enumerate all lessons sources">List every notes/*.md file. Categorize: (a) lessons docs, (b) design studies, (c) coord PRs, (d) deviation notes (task-XXX-deviations.md × 40+), (e) drift notes (wave-XX-drift-XX.md × 4), (f) session handoffs.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Extract each lesson">For each source file, extract concrete lessons in a normalized shape: {source-file, source-section, finding-id (F1/F2/...), title, symptom, root-cause, fix-applied (yes/no + where), landing-spot (code|archtest|skill|design.md|deployment-guide|prereqs.md|new-adr|new-task), effort-estimate, blocks-e2e (yes/no + reason), dependencies (list of other lessons or tasks)}. Store as YAML/JSON in an intermediate file — this is punch-list input.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Identify unapplied set">Compare each lesson's fix-applied field against actual repository state (grep for the fix, check design.md/skill.md for cited amendments). Produce the unapplied subset — this is the punch list.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Formalize PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md">Author docs/guides/PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md. Decision: markdown-with-YAML-frontmatter vs markdown-plus-sibling-YAML at scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml. Recommendation: sibling YAML (cleaner separation of concerns — YAML is machine-parseable, markdown is human-readable rendering with same data). Justify choice in file header per §11 template. Enumerate every prerequisite from owner's SESSION 5 list + any surfaced during Step 2 audit: SPE container-type + owning app, Office add-in Entra apps, Copilot bot Entra apps, Power BI service principals, Azure subscription (EA/MCA), OpenAI TPM quota bumps for frontier models, resource-provider registration on fresh subs, tenant-shared-domain registrations, etc. For each: {name, scope (tenant/sub/env/customer), how-to (link or inline recipe), frequency (once-per-X), programmatic-check-recipe (if possible — az/pac/graph command that returns present/absent/version), owner (who does it — Spaarke platform admin / customer admin), consequence-of-absence}.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Design provisioning-run structure">Author notes/provisioning-run-structure-design.md. Specify: (a) folder layout provisioning-runs/{customerId}-{runId}/ + INDEX.md; (b) file templates for CLAUDE.md (per-run AI context: loads shared context + per-run intake), intake.md (analog of spec — 4 required inputs + operator's decisions), prerequisites-check.md (Step 0.5 output archived per run), preflight-report.md (H0 output), handler-log.md (analog of current-task.md — live handler progress), manual-gates.md (H0.5/H8/H11 gate log), handoff-report.md (final report — supersedes today's runs/{runId}.md), lessons-learned.md (mandatory Step 7 postmortem); (c) INDEX.md schema (like projects/INDEX.md: customerId | runId | tenancyModel | profile | status | started | ended | lessons-count | link); (d) .claude/patterns/provisioning/ scaffolding proposal (patterns to seed: rbac-grant.md, kv-secret-naming.md, sweep-legacy-artifacts.md, etc.). Reference the coding-project pattern's structural principles (root CLAUDE.md §7 + task-create SKILL.md).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Design agent autonomy">Author notes/provisioning-run-agent-autonomy-design.md. Enumerate the current interactive gates in /provision-environment (Step 1 intake, Step 3 confirmation, Step 5 manual gates). For each, classify: (a) must-stay-interactive (SPE 24h clock, admin consent verification per NFR-11), (b) can-auto-advance-with-verification (backoff-poll L2 REST for idempotent re-runs), (c) can-batch-upfront (Step 1 intake collected via JSON blob if operator specifies --batch mode). Propose --batch flag for /provision-environment + JSON intake schema. Note operator-identity NFR-11 constraint still binds (agent runs UNDER operator's AAD context, not SP).</step>
    <step order="7" name="Author punch list">Author notes/task-202-punch-list.md. Table format: {lesson-id, source-doc, title, landing-spot, effort-h, blocks-e2e, dependencies, task-203-subphase}. Sort by blocks-e2e DESC then effort ASC. Task 203 executes against this table in order. Include NEW lessons surfaced during 202 audit — do NOT limit to pre-existing lessons.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Update task 186 escalation">Edit projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/tasks/186-real-phase-f-e2e-acceptance-rerun.poml to add explicit pre-check trigger: "if task-202-punch-list.md has any blocks-e2e=YES row with fix-applied=NO, abort task 186 and defer to task 203". Preserves existing escalation triggers.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Update TASK-INDEX + current-task.md">Add row for task 202 to TASK-INDEX.md (Phase Pre-Live-Fire section — NEW). Add placeholder row for task 203 (blocked on 202 completion). Update current-task.md: SESSION 5 handoff → task 202 in-progress → task 203 pending → task 186 blocked. Update Quick Recovery block accordingly.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Commit">Commit all in ONE atomic commit with detailed message: "docs(customer-provisioning): task 202 — pre-live-fire lessons audit + PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md formalization + provisioning-run structure design + task-203 punch list". Include lessons-count, unapplied-count, priority-ordering, task-203 handoff summary in commit body.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If audit surfaces a lesson requiring ADR amendment (path B per CLAUDE.md §6.5) — specifically SESSION 5 Lesson 3 (multi-tenant Dataverse routing at DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs:39 reading single Dataverse:ServiceUrl at DI setup time, incompatible with Model 1's per-tenant Dataverse design in model1-shared.bicep) — STOP and file the ADR Tension via design.md path B protocol. Do NOT silently work around in the punch list. This is a design decision that gates whether Model 1 shared BFF is architecturally viable as designed.</trigger>
    <trigger>If audit surfaces &gt;20 unapplied lessons blocking E2E, escalate to owner for prioritization — task 203's scope may need splitting into 203a/203b/203c to stay tractable (each &lt;24 hours effort).</trigger>
    <trigger>If PROVISIONING-PREREQUISITES.md's enumeration requires prerequisites we (Spaarke) have no way to programmatically check (e.g., legal-review sign-off for a customer contract) — flag with owner-review row in the YAML + prose warning in the markdown. Do NOT invent a fake check.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the provisioning-run structure design surfaces an obviously-better pattern than the coding-project analog (e.g., Cosmos-persisted per-run state instead of file-based) — note it in the design memo as a decision-record entry but DEFAULT to file-based analog per owner directive 2026-08-24 (parallel structure aids operator understanding).</trigger>
  </escalation>

